Subject: Composite Scheme of Amalgamation and Arrangement (Scheme) -
Receipt of MCA Order approving the Scheme

 

Dear All

 

This is with reference to the Composite Scheme of Amalgamation and
Arrangement amongst Gujarat State Petroleum Corporation Limited
("GSPC"/"Transferor Company 1"), Gujarat State Petronet Limited ("GSPL"/
"Transferor Company 2"), GSPC Energy Limited ("GEL"/ "Transferor Company
3"), Gujarat Gas Limited ("GGL"/ "Transferee Company"/ "Demerged Company")
and GSPL Transmission Limited ("GTL"/ "Resulting Company") and their
respective shareholders under sections 230 to 232 and other applicable
provisions of the Companies Act, 2013 ("Scheme"). The draft Scheme was
approved by the Board of Directors of all the above companies in their
meetings held on 30th August, 2024. 

Pursuant to the Scheme, the business undertakings of GSPC, GSPL and GEL
shall be amalgamated into GGL and, concurrently, the gas transmission
business undertaking being the business of laying, building, owning,
expanding and operating natural gas pipelines ("Gas Transmission Business
Undertaking"), shall be demerged into GTL.

We are pleased to inform that the Company has received Final Order
approving the Composite Scheme of Arrangement from the Ministry of
Corporate Affairs, New Delhi (MCA) on 17th April, 2026. 

Upon the Scheme becoming effective, the transactions of amalgamations and
demerger under the Scheme shall be implemented in the following order; 

A.	GSPC shall amalgamate into GGL with effect from Amalgamation
Appointed Date. 
B.	GSPL shall amalgamate into GGL with effect from Amalgamation
Appointed Date. 
C.	GEL shall amalgamate into GGL with effect from Amalgamation
Appointed Date.  

 

(The "Amalgamation Appointed Date" i.e., the date with effect from which
the accounting effect of Amalgamation shall be carried out in the books of
GGL is 1st April, 2024.)

 

D.	The gas transportation business carried on by GSPL & GGL shall be
demerged into GTL with effect from Demerger Appointed Date. 

 

(The "Demerged Appointed Date" i.e., the date with effect from which the
accounting effect of the Demerger shall be carried out in the books of GGL
and GTL is 1st April, 2025.)      

E.	Further, the name of Gujarat Gas Limited shall be changed to
Gujarat Energy Ltd. pursuant to the Scheme. 

The effective date for the Scheme is the filing of certified copy of MCA
Order with the Registrar of Companies, Ministry of Corporate Affairs.

Once the Scheme is made effective, you will again be notified regarding
the Effective Date of the Scheme. 

 

Kindly take note of the same. 

 

Best Regards

Nayan Simariya

M (P)

 

 




